\ Workload fixture for `make aot-symbol-verify`. Exercises AOT symbol-naming
\ categories with enough CPU work that perf and samply produce samples on the
\ named functions, so the verbatim-asm-name policy is observable in profiler
\ output. The `aot-asm-name-check` target already verifies `nm` covers every
\ category; this fixture's purpose is the profiler-level evidence.
\
\ Names below intentionally include `?`, `-`, and `>` to drive the
\ verbatim-preservation policy through the profiler stacks.

parse-json?: ( n -- result ) [
  0 swap [ 1 + ] times
] ;

>foo: ( n -- result ) [
  0 swap [ 2 + ] times
] ;

pick-quot: ( n ? -- result ) [
  [ 0 swap [ 3 + ] times ]
  [ 0 swap [ 4 + ] times ]
  if
] ;

10000000 parse-json? .
10000000 >foo .
10000000 t pick-quot .
10000000 f pick-quot .
